# Frontend

Server data uses TanStack Query. A household switch or theme uses React Context. Form fields and open/closed panels use `useState`.

Order in a component file: imports, props interface, hooks, early returns for loading, error, and empty, then the main render. `loading.tsx` mirrors the screen. Wrap a chart or dense table in an error boundary. Images use `next/image`.

Forms use React Hook Form, `zodResolver`, and shadcn `FormField`. Schemas stay in `types/[feature]/`. Mutations invalidate `queryKeys` in `onSuccess` and report errors through `useGlobalErrorHandler`.

Screen copy follows `docs/ui/README.md` and lives in `messages/en.json` / `messages/es.json` (next-intl). The person sees "You can spend" / "Puedes gastar", "Bills" / "Cuentas", "Goals" / "Metas", "Spending" / "Gastos", "Payday" / "Día de pago", and "Keep at least" / "Conservar al menos". They never see envelope, waterfall, tier, solvency, discretionary, tenant, or safe-to-spend in either language.

- New user-facing strings go in the message catalogs, not inline in components. Keep `en` and `es` keys in parity.
- UI language is per person (`users.preferred_locale`); URLs stay unprefixed (D17). Pass `useLocale()` into `formatMoney` / `formatShortDate`.
- One idea per screen. One filled button. Hide an action the role cannot perform. Do not show it disabled.
- The hero amount always shows cents. Other amounts drop `.00`. Dates follow the active locale, never ISO.
- Paper `#F4F1EA`, ink `#1C1917`. Green is only the hero when today is inside its pace. The filled button stays ink.
- The layout is one centered column at every width. Do not add a desktop dashboard.

```tsx
// ❌ engine vocabulary or hardcoded English
<p>Discretionary safe-to-spend</p>
<p>You can spend</p>

// ✅ catalog key
<p>{t("canSpend")}</p>
```
